{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 with multiprofile (avgpool) achieves 0.650 vs 0.520 for singleprofile — a ~13-point jump — while pca_n2000 singleprofile only reaches 0.485. Aggregation method (avgpool vs transformer) is nearly irrelevant (0.650 vs 0.653). The key uncertainty is whether the multiprofile benefit is a general property of having multiple profiles per cell or is specific to scvi_n200's learned latent representation. Question: Does pca_n2000 also gain substantially from multiprofile? config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean single-variable change from config_001 (pca_n2000, singleprofile), isolating the multiprofile effect for this encoder. Why this is the best next experiment: it directly tests whether multiprofile is a broadly applicable design principle or an encoder-specific interaction, which determines whether we should prioritize exploring multiprofile with other encoders (scgpt) or focus on optimizing the scvi_n200 + multiprofile pipeline (e.g., via multimodal fusion). This one experiment reduces the most uncertainty about the dominant design axis identified so far."
}

